<!--
    Ukrainian, polite "ви". DRAFT pending native-speaker review. Translated from the
    English source.
    - "ви" takes plural agreement, so verbs stay gender-neutral; first-person text about
      the author avoids gendered past tense ("Mood Cairns з’явився…").
    - Plurals use all four categories: one (1, 21, …), few (2-4, 22-24, …),
      many (0, 5-20, 25-30, …) and other (fractions; genitive singular).
    - The apostrophe is the typographic ’ (U+2019), which needs no XML escaping.
    - The rolling-average days use the invariant abbreviation "дн.", since that number
      is not the one driving the plural.
    Source: values/strings.xml.
-->
